  "id": "Compound::DB00695 - Gene::759",
  "verbalization": "Furosemide, a loop diuretic, is shown to bind to Ca14 and Ca2, two calcium-binding proteins, which are involved in the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide and carbonate dehydratase activity, respectively. These pathways are all associated with Ca1, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Furosemide may influence calcium homeostasis. The evidence indicates that Furosemide's interaction with Ca14 and Ca2 could modulate the activity of Ca1, potentially affecting cellular processes involving calcium regulation. The overlapping roles of Ca14 and Ca2 in the same pathway, coupled with the direct binding of Furosemide to these proteins, suggests a plausible mechanism by which Furosemide might influence Ca1 function. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Furosemide and Ca1, particularly through the modulation of calcium-related enzymatic activities.",
